<div class="guide-body">

  <h2 id="team">What's a Team Made Of?</h2>
  <p>Every match is scored across five categories — your team fields an athlete (or pair) in each:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Men's Singles</strong> and <strong>Women's Singles</strong> — one athlete each, head-to-head against the same category on the other team.</li>
    <li><strong>Men's Doubles</strong> and <strong>Women's Doubles</strong> — a same-gender pair, competing as one combined score.</li>
    <li><strong>Mixed Doubles</strong> — one man and one woman, paired together.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>There's no fixed roster size carved in stone — plenty of teams start with a handful of people covering multiple categories, and grow from there. Your gym decides who competes where, week to week.</p>

  <h2 id="gates">The 4 Gates — 12 Exercises</h2>
  <p>Every match moves through four gates in order. The first three each hold three exercises; the fourth is a combined sprint finish.</p>

  <div class="table-wrap" style="margin-top:1rem;">
    <table>
      <tr><th>Gate</th><th>Exercise</th><th>Benchmark</th></tr>
      <tr><td rowspan="3" style="font-weight:700;color:var(--forest);">1 — Posterior Chain</td><td>Ski Erg</td><td>800m</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Trap Bar Deadlift</td><td>84kg (M) / 54kg (W) × 30 reps</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Lunges</td><td>20kg (M) / 10kg (W) med ball × 10 × 8m lengths (80m)</td></tr>
      <tr><td rowspan="3" style="font-weight:700;color:var(--forest);">2 — Lower Body</td><td>Bike (Stationary)</td><td>1,500m</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Goblet Squat (DB)</td><td>25kg (M) / 17.5kg (W) × 30 reps</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Burpee Box Jump-Overs</td><td>60cm box × 40 reps</td></tr>
      <tr><td rowspan="3" style="font-weight:700;color:var(--forest);">3 — Upper Body</td><td>Assault Bike</td><td>80cal (M) / 50cal (W)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>DB Push Press</td><td>15kg (M) / 10kg (W) × 30 reps</td></tr>
      <tr><td>DB Snatch</td><td>15kg (M) / 10kg (W) × 30 reps, alternating</td></tr>
      <tr><td rowspan="3" style="font-weight:700;color:var(--forest);">4 — Sprint Finish</td><td>Wall Balls</td><td>6kg (M) / 4kg (W) × 50 reps</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Russian Twist</td><td>10kg (M) / 6kg (W) med ball × 30 each side</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Row 500m</td><td>First to finish wins</td></tr>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-top:.8rem;">Doubles and Mixed Doubles pairs are judged against the exact same benchmark as singles — a pair puts up one combined score, not two separate ones added together.</p>

  <h2 id="scoring">Scoring an Exercise — Gates 1–3</h2>
  <p>Every exercise in the first three gates works the same way:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Hit the benchmark → 1 point.</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Beat your direct opponent in that category → 1 more point</strong> (only available on top of hitting the benchmark).</li>
    <li><strong>Miss the benchmark → 0 points</strong>, regardless of how your opponent did.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="guide-callout">
    Max <strong>2 points</strong> per exercise, per category. Nine exercises across Gates 1–3 = up to <strong>18 points</strong> before you even reach the sprint finish.
  </div>

  <h3>Gate 4 — The Sprint Finish</h3>
  <p>All three exercises are combined into one timed, all-out effort. No per-exercise points here — it's about finishing, and finishing first.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Complete all three → 3 points.</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Finish first → 3 more points.</strong> Winner takes all — no partial credit for second.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="match">Winning a Match — The Season Table</h2>
  <p>Add up every exercise and Gate 4 result for both teams, across all five categories, and whoever has the higher total wins the match. That's what decides who wins on the day.</p>
  <p>For the <strong>season standings</strong>, that result converts into league points — same idea as most team sports:</p>
  <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top:1rem;">
    <div class="card">
      <h4 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--forest);font-size:1.1rem;margin-bottom:.6rem;">Win the match</h4>
      <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;">Higher total across all categories and gates.</p>
      <span class="pill">3 points</span>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h4 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--forest);font-size:1.1rem;margin-bottom:.6rem;">Lose, but finish everything</h4>
      <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;">Every athlete/pair attempted every exercise and every Gate 4 sprint.</p>
      <span class="pill">1 point</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p style="margin-top:1rem;">Lose <em>and</em> don't complete every station — a no-show or a DNF partway through — and the match is worth <strong>0 points</strong> in the table. Showing up and finishing always counts for something; not finishing doesn't.</p>

  <h2 id="season">The Season</h2>
  <p>A typical season runs <strong>6 weeks</strong>. With 4 teams in a region, everyone plays each other twice — one match a week, every week, home and away style. Your season table tracks match points, wins/draws/losses, and total points scored for and against (the tiebreaker when two teams are level on match points) — updated the moment results are entered on match day.</p>

